        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Midnight Oil, Switchfoot\n- People: Peter Garrett, Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, Drew Shirley\n- Songs: \"Beds Are Burning\"\n- Albums: \"Diesel and Dust\", \"Oh! Gravity.\"\n- Events: Oh! Gravity. Tour\n- Places: Sydney, San Diego, California\n- Topics: band formation, band membership, music releases, concert tours\n\nFacts:\n- By late 1976, Peter Garrett moved to Sydney to complete his law degree.\n- By late 1976, the band Farm changed its name to Midnight Oil by drawing the name from a hat.\n- Switchfoot is an American alternative rock band from San Diego, California.\n- The members of Switchfoot are Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, and Drew Shirley.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" is a 1987 song by the Australian rock band Midnight Oil.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" was the first track on Midnight Oil's album \"Diesel and Dust\".\n- Oh! Gravity. Tour is a 2007 concert tour by Switchfoot.\n- Switchfoot held the Oh! Gravity. Tour to promote its sixth studio album, \"Oh! Gravity.\"",
